From 9690aa76891e30a652e027a3ab520aafe87d04d9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Jouve <adrien.jouve@adn-dev.fr>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 16:45:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] feat(plugins): a plugin may bring a page, a door and a
 drawer (spec 180)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A plugin was handed a logger, an event bus, settings and devices — right for
turning a protocol into devices, and the whole surface. Three things followed:
it could show nothing beyond its settings form, could be reached by nobody but
an admin, and had nowhere to keep state (`pluginDir` looks like the place and
is a trap: an update removes it and unpacks the new release in its place).

Three generic capabilities, no domain learned by the core:

- `ui: { entry, label, icon }` in the manifest — the SPA imports that ES module
  at /plugins/<id>/page and calls mount(container, ctx), with an api() already
  bound to /api/v1/plugins/<id>/page/*. Plain DOM, not React: a plugin builds
  against its own dependencies. Assets under /plugin-ui/<id>/*, confined to the
  entry's directory, by extension allowlist.
- `publicTree: true` — makes an anonymous tree at /p/<id>/* buildable and
  nothing more: it answers the same 404 as an undeclared plugin until an admin
  opens it from the plugin's sheet (core setting, audit-logged). Then 60/min per
  IP, X-Robots-Tag noindex, 30 s then 504, and Set-Cookie from a plugin refused.
- `deps.dataDir` = data/plugins/<id>/ — created before the factory runs, never
  touched by install, update or uninstall, and now carried by the backup.

Both surfaces hand the plugin an allowlist of headers rather than the request:
the caller's bearer stays in the core, and `authorization` reaches the public
surface only, where it is the plugin's own token.

Tests: 23 route cases, 7 on the page listing, 3 on getDataDir, 2 on the backup,
6 on the SPA page. Docs: plugin-development (EN/FR), api-reference (EN/FR),
specs/180 and both indexes.
