From 904a7a137cdd92b38c428d8211a60e324c455b4e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adrienJouve <adrien.jouve@adn-dev.fr>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 08:52:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] feat(plugins): a page may ask for the main navigation
 (spec 180 R1.6.bis)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Every plugin page was filed under Administration, beside Plugins and Logs.
That is right for a page configured once, and wrong for one used every
week: who may open the gate on Tuesday is not an admin screen.

`ui.placement: "main"` lists the page in the main navigation after
Analyse. The default — and anything unexpected — stays `admin`, so no
existing page moves. Placement changes where the entry is drawn, never who
may see it: the list and the page stay admin-only.

The desktop sidebar and the mobile drawer place pages from one split
(`plugin-page-nav.ts`), so they cannot disagree. Two things found on the
way, both from the first version of this spec:

- the mobile drawer listed no plugin page at all, so on a phone a plugin's
  page was unreachable; it now lists them where the sidebar does;
- the top bar named every plugin page « Plugins » (the route starts with
  /plugins); it now uses the page's own label.

A main page's route lives under /plugins like the admin screens, so the
sidebar no longer opens Administration on it.
