From 6d6869338af4f481cb84538d13b393f1906b24f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adrienJouve <adrien.jouve@adn-dev.fr>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:07:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] feat(plugins): a plugin page may be linked from an
 equipment's own page (spec 180 R1.6.ter)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A plugin that holds something about an equipment — who may open this
gate — had no way to say so where the owner looks at that equipment. Its
page was reachable from the menu only.

`ui.equipmentLink: { types }` puts a card on the page of every equipment
of those types, beside the core's own panels (confirmation before action,
timed command). The card links to `/plugins/<id>/page?equipment=<id>`,
and the page module now receives the query string as `ctx.params`.

The card's sentence and the link's words are the plugin's: the core asks
`GET equipment-link?equipmentId=&lang=` on the plugin's page tree and
prints the `{ text, action }` it answers, because only the plugin knows
what it holds. A plugin that does not answer still gets its card, with
its page's label and a plain « Open ». Admin-only, like the page.
